---
// Blog: the launch post, and a pointer to the changelog for everything since.
// The launch version is read from docs/version-history.md, never typed.
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Card from '../components/Card.astro';
import Section from '../components/Section.astro';
import { readRepoFile } from '../lib/repo.mjs';
import { GH_URL } from '../lib/site-nav.mjs';

const opened = /public repository opens at \*\*v(\d+\.\d+\.\d+)\*\*/.exec(
  readRepoFile('docs/version-history.md'),
);
if (!opened) throw new Error('docs/version-history.md no longer states the version the public repository opened at');
const launch = opened[1];
---

<Base
  title="Blog"
  description="The skep launch post. Everything since the launch is in the changelog."
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap narrow stack">
      <p class="eyebrow t-micro">Blog</p>
      <h1 class="t-h2">One post, and a changelog</h1>
      <p class="t-lead prose-width">
        There is one post here: the launch. What has changed since is recorded release by release
        in the changelog, which is generated from the project’s version history.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Section band narrow eyebrow="Launch" title="The launch post">
    <article class="card post">
      <p class="t-micro c-mut"><time datetime="2026-07-30">2026-07-30</time> · Launch</p>
      <h3 class="t-h3">skep <span class="mono">v{launch}</span>: the public launch</h3>
      <p class="prose-width">
        skep opened as a local supervisor for coding agents: the agent works in a disposable
        worktree, skep re-verifies what it claims, and the patch waits for your approval. It had
        been in daily use since mid-July 2026 and arrived as one <code>pipx install skep</code>.
      </p>
      <p class="prose-width t-small c-mut">
        That is the project as it launched. It has changed since: one policy engine, external
        agents always in the sandbox, a pinned verify command, opt-in auto-landing. For what it
        does now, read <a class="c-green" href="/how-it-works.html">how it works</a>.
      </p>
      <div class="row">
        <a class="link-arrow" href={`${GH_URL}/releases/tag/v${launch}`}>Release notes on GitHub</a>
        <a class="link-arrow" href="https://anmolnoor.com/blog/skep-is-live">The launch post, in skep’s own words</a>
      </div>
    </article>
  </Section>

  <Section narrow eyebrow="Since then" title="What changed since">
    <div class="grid grid-2">
      <Card title="Changelog" icon="history" href="/changelog.html">
        Published releases, newest first, with the work each one carried.
      </Card>
      <Card title="Version history" icon="file-text" href="/docs/version-history.html">
        The round-by-round record the changelog is generated from, including the releases
        before the changelog starts.
      </Card>
    </div>
  </Section>
</Base>

<style>
  .post {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--s-4);
  }
</style>
